{"name":"Rum Punch","hex":"#aa423a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Romanian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spirit distilled from various preparations of sugarcane, particularly fermented cane sugar and molasses.","A serving of rum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rum"},{"term":"punch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hit or strike with one's fist.","A blow from something other than the fist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike with one's fist.","To herd (cattle) as a cowboy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rum Punch","blocks":[{"text":"Rum Punch is a 1992 novel written by Elmore Leonard that was adapted into the film Jackie Brown (1997) by director Quentin Tarantino."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Rum_punch_first_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum_Punch","wikidata":"Q3281349"},{"title":"Punch (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"The term punch refers to a wide assortment of drinks, both alcoholic and non-alcoholic, generally containing fruits or fruit juice. The drink was introduced from the Indian subcontinent to England by employees of the East India Company in the late 17th century. Punch is usually served at parties in large, wide bowls, known as punch bowls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG/330px-Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punch_(drink)","wikidata":"Q1121224"},{"title":"Rum","blocks":[{"text":"Rum is a liquor made by fermenting and then distilling sugarcane molasses or sugarcane juice. The distillate, initially a clear liquid, is often aged in barrels. Rum originated in the Caribbean in the 17th century, where it was likely first created by enslaved people on sugar plantations, but has come to be produced in nearly every major sugar-producing region of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/A_glass_of_rum.jpg/330px-A_glass_of_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum","wikidata":"Q83376"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/500px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/1280px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg/500px-Southern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Southern Bourbon Punch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouthern_Bourbon_Punch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bowle.JPG/500px-Bowle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bowle.JPG/1280px-Bowle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bowle.JPG/500px-Bowle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fruit punch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABowle.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/1891_era_bottle_of_punsch.png/250px-1891_era_bottle_of_punsch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/1891_era_bottle_of_pu